 const DECISION_FOLLOWUPS={"7":["The existing evidence joins the hearing record. Mara and Tessa remain available as witnesses.","Kael accepts the question. He will answer for the order without asking you to excuse it.","The hearing is recorded. Silence does not imply forgiveness or agreement."],"9":["The marked exit becomes the shared route. Rowan follows your directions instead of carrying you without asking.","You release the marked lock while Rowan holds the rope steady. Both of you can leave.","You count the steps together. The escape is a joint task, not a romantic debt."],"10":["The route is checked as a fallback. At the checkpoint, a patrol turns toward the manor; you receive a safe return message before rejoining the others.","Mara keeps the exit available while you remain in the valley. Staying is not a relationship promise.","The report is kept as a lead to verify, not proof that Rowan has already found Iris."],"11":["The staff preserve the footprints. Accepting or refusing a dance cannot erase this evidence.","Rowan checks the route without treating an unknown footprint as proof of guilt.","A dated image preserves the marks for later review."],"15":["The shard is sealed as evidence. The recorded kiss remains a forgery, never a real intimate memory.","The projection record is preserved before the mirror is broken. No consent has been given.","Iris keeps a silver-dust sample for examination. The evidence chain remains open."],"17":["The account is kept anonymous. Publication must not expose the trapped witnesses.","Identities are protected. You can still challenge the oath without publishing private names.","Mara records the safety questions before anyone attempts to release a sealed voice."],"18":["The assignments are recorded: Kael guards, Rowan investigates, Lucien researches.","The assignments are recorded: Kael investigates, Rowan guards, Lucien researches.","The assignments are recorded: Kael guards, Rowan researches, Lucien investigates."],"19":["Standing beside him is recorded as support, without a romantic promise.","The existing archive record is submitted. It will be checked against the witnesses.","The objections are dated and recorded for the next hearing."],"21":["The preserved projection record is compared with the missing audio. Witness testimony provides a fallback.","The access log is compared with the original record. Witness testimony provides a fallback.","The protected testimony is heard without disclosing private addresses. An investigation still needs verified evidence."],"24":["Your opening line is saved. You can write a fuller note in your own words later in this chapter.","Your opening line is saved. Continuing the adventure does not require a partner.","Your opening line is saved. Your own life is a complete future."],"25":["The delay creates time to break the mechanism. It does not permit a kiss or any other contact.","Your refusal stands. The team works on the mechanism without demanding a partner choice.","The three men leave for their separate tasks. None of them asks for contact as payment."],"27":["Kael laughs at his own toast. This ordinary memory is kept without assuming a kiss.","You make another slice together. Nobody treats breakfast as consent to live together.","The shelter plans stay on the table. Friendship is enough reason to share this work."],"28":["The journey is a discussion. No one has moved away or agreed to a relationship by default.","Separate lives and future visits remain open for a later agreement.","Rowan accepts your friendship. His investigation continues for its own sake."],"29":["Lucien includes the course in his plans. Teaching does not restore foresight.","A shared journal can preserve what each person agrees to record. It cannot force a memory back.","The quiet evening needs neither a test nor a prediction."],"30":["You open the future letter before making a relationship decision.","The chosen policy remains independent of the person you approach next.","Kael works on the garden platform, Rowan unloads supplies, and Lucien keeps his astronomy notebook. They each have a life beyond being chosen."]};
